From b26c98ea33839c00021c6872e97effe129dfef5e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 16:27:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 10/14] Say ALMOVA instead of wger in the app texts

The English, Portuguese and Brazilian Portuguese texts name ALMOVA where
they meant the app or its server: the login ("New to ALMOVA?"), the server
and token fields, the barcode, health sync and calculated value notes, and
the sync service screen, which no longer tells patients to check a
self-hosted PowerSync. The about text keeps the credit to wger, which
ALMOVA is built on. The Brazilian Portuguese file gets the texts it took
from English so far. Other languages keep the wger texts until they are
translated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01VRSTuUkoebWWM2DLbPZAvR
